        },
        {
          "height" : 15.9,
          "text" : "Measuring Folded Card Spacers for Model Rails",
          "width" : 297.8,
          "x" : 149.5,
          "y" : 88
        },
        {
          "height" : 12,
          "text" : "Anonymous Authors1",
          "width" : 91.8,
          "x" : 249.2,
          "y" : 140.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "Abstract",
          "width" : 44.5,
          "x" : 150.2,
          "y" : 174.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "A folded card spacer fixes the height of a model",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 192.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "rail above its baseboard. We measured spacers",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 204.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "folded from three card stocks in a single test slot",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 216.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "and compared the measured heights with a sim-",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 228.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "ple layer model. The model predicts the height",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 240.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "of a folded spacer to within a tenth of a millime-",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 252.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "tre when the crease allowance is taken from a",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 264.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "two-layer trial. We describe the slot, the mea-",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 276.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "surement procedure and the remaining sources",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 288.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "of error, and we list practical rules for choosing",
          "width" : 194.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 300.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "a card stock for a given rail height.",
          "width" : 138.9,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 312.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "rules. Earlier notes on layered card (Card Stock Bench and",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 176.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Model Rail Desk, 2024) and on gauge blocks (Scale Fixture",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 188.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 12,
          "text" : "Room, 2023) motivated the layer model used here.1",
          "width" : 205.7,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 199.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "1. Introduction",
          "width" : 76.8,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 345.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Paper models of railways need many small parts of exact",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 366.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "height. Rails, platform edges and signal bases all sit on",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 378.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "spacers, and a spacer that is too thick by a fraction of a",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 390.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "millimetre lifts a rail joint enough to derail a light wagon.",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 402.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Most builders cut spacers from card and fold them until",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 414
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "they reach the height they want (Model Rail Desk, 2025).",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 426
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Folding is quick and needs no tools, but the height of a",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 437.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "folded spacer is not simply the sum of the card thicknesses:",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 449.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "each crease adds a small allowance, and the allowance de-",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 461.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "pends on the card and on how firmly the crease is pressed.",
          "width" : 232.4,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 473.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "This note reports a bench trial of folded spacers. Our aims",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 491.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "were:",
          "width" : 22.1,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 503.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "2. Method",
          "width" : 51.8,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 227.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "2.1. The test slot",
          "width" : 68.9,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 248.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "The slot was cut into a block of laminated board and lined",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 266.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "with a strip of thin brass so that the card could not dent the",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 278.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "walls. A sliding rail of known height rests on top of the",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 290.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "spacer, and the height is read from a scale on the side of the",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 302.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "block. The block was clamped to the bench throughout the",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 314.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "trial so that the scale did not move between readings.",
          "width" : 211.4,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 326.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Each spacer was inserted with its folded edge towards the",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 344.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "back of the slot. The rail was lowered onto it and left for",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 356.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "ten seconds before the reading was taken, because a freshly",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 368.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "folded spacer springs back slowly. Three readings were",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 380.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "taken for each spacer, removing and reinserting it between",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 392.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "readings.",
          "width" : 36.2,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 404.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "2.2. Layer model",
          "width" : 71.2,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 429.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "We model the height h of a spacer with n layers of card of",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 448.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "thickness t as",
          "width" : 54,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 460.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.7,
          "text" : "h= n t + (n− 1) c,",
          "width" : 82.1,
          "x" : 383.4,
          "y" : 474.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.7,
          "text" : "(1)",
          "width" : 11.6,
          "x" : 529.8,
          "y" : 474.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "•",
          "width" : 3.5,
          "x" : 66.9,
          "y" : 527.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "to measure the height of spacers with two to six lay-",
          "width" : 214.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 527.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "ers in one fixed slot;",
          "width" : 81.3,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 539.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "where c is the crease allowance added by each fold. The",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 494.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "allowance is found from a two-layer trial, for which Equa-",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 506.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 12.4,
          "text" : "tion (1) gives c = h2− 2t. The same model was used for",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 518.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "the gauge block of Scale Fixture Room (2023), where it",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 530.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "predicted the height of folded board well for up to four lay-",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 542.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "ers.",
          "width" : 14.1,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 554.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "•",
          "width" : 3.5,
          "x" : 66.9,
          "y" : 558.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "to compare the measurements with a layer model that",
          "width" : 214.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 558.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "adds a crease allowance; and",
          "width" : 115.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 570.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "•",
          "width" : 3.5,
          "x" : 66.9,
          "y" : 589.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "to give simple rules for choosing a card stock for a",
          "width" : 214.1,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 589.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "target height.",
          "width" : 52.4,
          "x" : 75.4,
          "y" : 601.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Section 2 describes the slot and the procedure, Section 3",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 625.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "reports the measurements, and Section 4 summarises the",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 637.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "Card thickness.",
          "width" : 68,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 580.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "The thickness t was measured with a",
          "width" : 156.1,
          "x" : 385.4,
          "y" : 580.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "dial gauge on ten single sheets of each stock, and the mean",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 307.4,
          "y" : 592.9
        },
